-- One-time data update: China Wall Twister gets a new layout.
--
-- Its own layout and opening (Moses, 15 Nov 2026: the World Tour re-layouts):
-- until now it was physically the same track as Rio Jungle Rumble. Out through
-- a gate in the Wall (the tunnel-launch start, the field let go in waves) past
-- the pandas and lanterns, along the Wall and down its steps, a sweep past the
-- pagoda, the board-game run, the fortune-cat hairpin, up over a ridge and
-- through the dragon (the big feature and signature: a long drop through its
-- body, in at the tail and out of the mouth), the pagoda spiral, S-bends past
-- the rice terraces and on to the Temple of Heaven. Its name, slug, look and
-- past races stay. Its track record, country records and players' personal
-- bests start again from now (tracks.records_since); past results stay. Races
-- already run keep their stored replays and play back exactly as they ran.
--
-- Generated from src/game/physicsTracks.js by scripts/physics-track-sql.js --relayout.
-- Only the China Wall Twister track row changes.

